{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1290768-an-alternate-aeon-setting","id":1290768,"title":"An Alternate Aeon Setting.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-22T08:09:41-08:00","id":1290768,"title":"An Alternate Aeon Setting.","content":"Basically, this idea is a setting patch, but one that works. The key alteration is in the past. First, the Terragen fade out as a group, keeping a group of narcissistic wannabe monsters locked in eternal adolescence together as a coherent force was never in the cards. With Clarion focused on taking out anyone between him and Divis it simply shortened the group's life and vitality dramatically. Second, from the Inspiration Age on, empowered people were getting into space and going off to explore and settle new worlds. Third, Divis, unable to get over old obsessions or admit any serious weaknesses period, does something idiotic. He tries to roll back time and erase the history he rejects.<br /> <br /> The Aberrant Wars are the shadow of Divis Mal's death/collapse. The fantasies of his dying mind burned into humanity psyches. The warped mess that his the Aeon setting is humanity slowly coming out of the shadows of Divis Mal's deliriums<br /> .<br /> In this setting, the Doyne and Mister Saturday are linked. Who is the origin of whom is unclear, but they've been working as a team to warp humanity into a slave species they own.<br /> <br /> Large numbers of off-world settlements are spread throughout the galaxy. These represent all sorts of possibilities. Novas, Psions, Psiads, Inspired, etc...in many different types of settings.<br /> <br /> Note: Many people on Earth know that they live in the shadow of Dreams and Delirium, but what happens if the dream ends. These people call Divis Mal the Red King. And when the Red King wakes, what happens to his dreams? Best to keep the Red King asleep and the masses likewise because who knows what the alternative is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-22-2019, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T09:27:02-08:00","id":1290797,"title":"","content":"I like this. A lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T10:14:28-08:00","id":1290818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadryx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1290768-an-alternate-aeon-setting?p=1290797#post1290797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this. A lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank-you. Do you have ideas to add?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T13:51:11-08:00","id":1290896,"title":"","content":"I'll think on it. I'm not up on my Aberrant lore as much as I am with some other settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T13:52:36-08:00","id":1290897,"title":"","content":"Who was Mister Saturday?<br /> <br /> So Earth us got Hacked because Divis Mal was subconsciously Wanda Maximoffing/David Hallering the planet in a weird reality warping anemic wish fulfillment field? And since Adventure in there has been steady trickles of super scientists of all stripes making their way off planet to explore and colonize?<br /> <br /> So Aeon is the setting where Earth is only starting to dip out of the Red Kings influence but a lot of the world is afraid if they can survive the Red King Waking up or dying?<br /> <br /> Meanwhile humanity is healthy among the stars amidst several 100-200 year old colonies of varying sizes and varying distances away?<br /> <br /> And a mysterious force game humanity 8 Prometheus Chambers, to fight the Red King?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T17:27:06-08:00","id":1290938,"title":"","content":"Mr Saturday is a powerful Mesmerists in Adventure. If I am not wrong about the image is a black guy with top hat and evil smile...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T17:44:26-08:00","id":1290942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1290768-an-alternate-aeon-setting?p=1290938#post1290938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mr. Saturday is a powerful Mesmerists in Adventure. If I am not wrong about the image is a black guy with a top hat and an evil smile...</div> </div> </div> </div>Dead on, he influenced the incident that started the Inspiration age. He is subtle and focused, he wants to rule humanity forever. How he plans to do that isn't detailed but human free will clearly isn't part of his plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T20:26:10-08:00","id":1290983,"title":"","content":"I figured it was a Baron Samedi reference. The Doyen seem to Cheval superstitious cultures around the universe. I can dig it. If the Doyen turn their eye to Earth Early I can see them start by making a custom Gene surgeried Proxy who sold out the planet. Or even a Doyen who enjoys living in a body to subvert humanity in person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T01:03:53-08:00","id":1291032,"title":"","content":"Mr Saturday used to work to Hammersmith and got a part of his fortune when he died (that could mean he was planing the explosion). This means he was replaced by Sara Burahno?<br /> <br /> Can\u2019t remember if he was inspired before Hammersmith... but for sure he was an evil mastermind a la Baron Samedi... I think he even used voodoo stile on his powers...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T01:37:27-08:00","id":1291044,"title":"","content":"So was he only Mentioned in Adventure?<br /> <br /> I never Got Adventure, was Adventure treating the three types of Inspired similar to how Talents are now treated in the Corebook, with just some extra Knacks or Edges or Powers themed after their type?<br /> <br /> Like Mesmers didn\u2019t have Aptitudes and Modes Right? Their powers were more simplified?<br /> <br /> It would be hella interesting to have some secret Proxies around in the early 1900\u2019s. Hell now that I think about it why not just create secret Proxies as NPCs in any game, it\u2019s a fun character type and throws folks for a loop. Hell they don\u2019t even have to be human, imagine a Chromatic or Qin Secret Proxy!<br /> <br /> Hmm I want to start another thread now... the ideas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T06:16:03-08:00","id":1291110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1290768-an-alternate-aeon-setting?p=1291044#post1291044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So was he only Mentioned in Adventure?</div> </div> </div> </div>He was as detailed as the other major background villains.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I never Got Adventure, was Adventure treating the three types of Inspired similar to how Talents are now treated in the Corebook, with just some extra Knacks or Edges or Powers themed after their type? </div> </div> </div>There were Daredevils (proto-Talents), Stalwarts(proto-Novas), and Mesmerists (proto-Psions). The Daredevils are close in power level to Talents, sometimes less powerful, sometimes more. Both Stalwarts and Mesmerists are decidedly weaker than Novas, Psiads, or Psions. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like Mesmers didn\u2019t have Aptitudes and Modes Right? Their powers were more simplified? </div> </div> </div>They have Knacks. All Daredevils knacks cost two Inspiration points. Stalwarts and Mesmerists have one, two, and three point knacks. These are not linked like modes or aptitudes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would be hella interesting to have some secret Proxies around in the early 1900\u2019s. Hell now that I think about it why not just create secret Proxies as NPCs in any game, it\u2019s a fun character type and throws folks for a loop. Hell they don\u2019t even have to be human, imagine a Chromatic or Qin Secret Proxy! </div> </div> </div>Great idea. Maybe Divis Mal and Mercer are botched attempts to have secret proxies. The major villains of Adventure could be reworked as Secret Proxies or might simply be catspaw of the Doyne.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm I want to start another thread now... the ideas! </div> </div> </div>Go for it!!!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}